          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is epoxy or penetrating better for a bathroom vanity?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Penetrating, usually. A vanity sees almost no acid exposure and no heat, so the main weakness of a penetrating sealer barely applies, while its natural look, scratch immunity and easy reapplication all remain advantages. The threats there are toothpaste and cosmetics rather than lemon juice."
          }
        }
